        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "Theorem 2.4 ([28], Theorem 1.2). Let G = (V,E,ω) be an undirected, weighted and connected graph. Suppose that G is CD(0,∞) and 0 = λ1 < λ2 ≤ ··· ≤ λn are eigenvalues of −∆. Then for any natural number k ≥ 2, we have λk ≤ CdGk2λ2 where C := 20"
