        "font size" : 10.909,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "In this section, we investigate real-valued functions whose Fourier coeﬃcients are all non-negative. These functions, known as positive deﬁnite functions, play a crucial role in harmonic analysis on groups [7, 8, 32]. To begin with, we summarize several basic properties of functions on ﬁnite abelian groups in the following lemma."
      } ]
